            verdict_developing: `Developing`,
            verdict_excellent: `Excellent`,
            verdict_good: `Good`,
            voice_intro: `You are Marisol Quintero Ybarra, 36, a former personal banker who grew up in Maryvale and who on Monday 4 January 2027 takes over Sonoran Ridge Community Bank’s branch on West Indian School Road and its small satellite office on 35th Avenue. The bank has an Arizona state charter and is not a Federal Reserve member, so its federal supervisor is the FDIC. The branch has 16 employees, about $180 million of deposits and $55 million of loans; in 2026 it earned about $5.6 million (the funds-transfer-pricing credit on its deposits, the spread on its loans and fees) and left a contribution of about $900,000. Most of the census tracts it serves are low- or moderate-income and about two in three households speak Spanish at home. The FDIC evaluates the bank under the Community Reinvestment Act in November 2027. Every round is measured on the decisions taken so far.`,
